'''Zett Jukassa''' was a [[human]] [[Gender|male]] [[Padawan]] of the [[Jedi Order]] during the [[Republic Era|time]] of the [[Galactic Republic]]. He was present in the [[Jedi Archives]], the Order's [[library]] within the [[Imperial Palace|Jedi Temple]] on the [[planet]] [[Coruscant]], in [[22 BBY]]. Three [[Standard year|years]] later, in [[19 BBY]], [[Order 66]] was declared by the [[Dark Lord of the Sith|Sith Lord]] [[Darth Sidious]], leading to [[clone trooper]]s of the [[Grand Army of the Republic]] [[Operation: Knightfall|attacking]] the Jedi Temple. As Jukassa attempted to flee the siege, he came across several [[trooper]]s. Although he was able to incapacitate a number of them, Jukassa was [[Death|slain]] in battle by [[Clone Sergeant]] [[Fox (501st Legion)|Fox]] as [[Senator]] [[Bail Prestor Organa|Bail Organa]] watched.

==Biography==
{{Quote|No!|Bail Organa's reaction to Jukassa's death|<ref name="Episode III" />}}
Zett Jukassa was [[Reproduction|born]] around [[29 BBY]]<ref name="birth" /> and, after being [[Jedi training|trained]] as a [[Jedi]] of the [[Jedi Order]], he attained the rank of [[Padawan]]<ref name="DB Zett" /> during the [[Republic Era|time]] of the [[Galactic Republic]]. Prior to the [[First Battle of Geonosis|start]] of the [[Clone Wars]],<ref name="Episode II">{{Film|II}}</ref> in [[22 BBY]],<ref name="AOTC Date">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas: Updated Edition]]'' dates the events of {{Film|II}} to [[22 BBY]].</ref> Jukassa was present in the Order's [[library]], the [[Jedi Archives]], located in the [[Imperial Palace|Jedi Temple]] on the [[Core Worlds]] [[planet]] of [[Coruscant]]. As [[Jedi librarian]] [[Jocasta Nu]] conversed with [[Jedi Knight]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]], Jukassa walked up to Nu, who then attended to him after finishing with Kenobi<ref name="Episode II" /> as Jukassa understood the importance of a Jedi's studies.<ref name="pocket" />

[[File:Zett_Jukasa_Order_66.png|thumb|left|300px|Jukassa fights clone troopers during the execution of Order 66.]]
In [[19 BBY]],<ref name="Date" /> [[Supreme Chancellor]] [[Darth Sidious|Sheev Palpatine]], secretly the [[Dark Lord of the Sith|Sith Lord]] [[Darth]] Sidious, issued [[Order 66]] to the [[clone trooper]]s of the [[Grand Army of the Republic]], labeling the entire Jedi Order as [[Treason|traitors]] to the state. As such, Jukassa and his Jedi brethren were forced to fight for their lives when the [[Sith Lord]] [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]] and the Grand Army of the Republic's [[501st Legion]] [[Operation: Knightfall|stormed]] the Temple with orders to [[Great Jedi Purge|exterminate]] its inhabitants.<ref name="Episode III" /> Jukassa attempted to flee via one of the Temple [[hangar]]s,<ref name="HC 16">{{HelmetCollectionCite|16|Helmets}}</ref> but he ran into a group of [[Cloning|clone]] [[trooper]]s on the landing platform.<ref name="Episode III" /> The Padawan fought heroically against them<ref name="DB Zett" /> with his [[lightsaber]], executing a flip and [[Death|killing]] several clones,<ref name="Episode III" /> as well as striking down [[Clone Commander|Commander]] [[Appo]],<ref name="HC 16" /> before being shot and killed<ref name="Episode III" /> by [[Clone Sergeant]] [[Fox (501st Legion)|Fox]].<ref name="Fox">{{ForceCollection|Clone Sergeant Fox|star=4}}</ref> [[Senator]] [[Bail Prestor Organa|Bail Organa]] of the planet [[Alderaan]], who had arrived to investigate the disturbance at the Temple, witnessed the entire fight<ref name="Episode III" /> and was horrified by Jukassa's death.<ref name="DB Zett" />

In the same [[Standard year|year]],<ref name="Date MOF">{{MOFdate}}</ref> early in the [[Galactic Empire]]'s [[Imperial Era|reign]], Organa began [[Investigation into the framing of the Jedi|investigating]] the role of the Empire's leadership in the purge of the Jedi. He somberly remembered witnessing Jukassa's death, noting that Palpatine had claimed the massacre was a necessity and reflecting on the young ages of both the slain Jedi combatant and the clones he had attacked.<ref name="MOF">''[[Reign of the Empire: The Mask of Fear]]''</ref> In [[18 BBY]],<ref name="18 BBY">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of [[Ahsoka (novel)|''Ahsoka'']] to [[18 BBY]].</ref> Organa experienced [[Dream|nightmares]] about the night that he witnessed Jukassa die. In some versions of the dream, he was able to save the Padawan; in others, the clones shot Organa as well as Jukassa. When Organa learned of [[Ahsoka Tano|Jedi]] [[Raada Uprising|activity]] on the [[Outer Rim Territories]] [[moon]] of [[Raada]], it filled his [[heart]] with dread as he remembered the night of Order 66.<ref name="Ahsoka">[[Ahsoka (novel)|''Ahsoka'']]</ref>

==Personality and traits==
[[File:Appo_Jukassa.jpg|thumb|right|300px|Zett Jukassa wounded Commander Appo during the 501st Legion's assault on the Jedi Temple.]]
Though only a young Jedi at the [[time]] of Order 66, Zett Jukassa heroically fought back against the invading clone troopers<ref name="DB Zett" /> with the courage and determination of a Jedi Knight. Jukassa was committed to protecting the Jedi Order. He was a [[human]] [[Gender|male]] and stood at 1.57 [[meter]]s tall (5 [[Foot|feet]], one inch).<ref name="pocket" /> Jukassa had light skin, [[Color|blue]] [[eye]]s, and he wore a [[Padawan braid]] in his brown [[hair]].<ref name="Episode III" />

==Powers and abilities==
During the night of Order 66, Jukassa used his lightsaber to overwhelm a group of clone troopers.<ref name="Episode III" /> As a formidable warrior,<ref name="pocket" /> he was able to deflect [[blaster]] shots with his lightsaber, parrying several shots before being fatally wounded.<ref name="Episode III" />

==Equipment==
Jukassa wore simple, gray [[Jedi apparel|Jedi robes]] and carried a blue-bladed lightsaber.<ref name="pocket" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|Jett really did well. He likes to play, so when we rehearsed with him we would have half an hour of playing and half an hour of rehearsing. I think he was keeping a whole load back. He actually nailed it in the first few days and he just wanted to come and play, because when he went on the set he did it in his sleep. There was no trouble at all for him.|Nick Gillard on the performance of Jett Lucas|<ref name="StarWars.com">{{SWArchive|url=episode-iii/bts/profile/f20051221/index.html|text=The Force Runs Strong In This Family: Jett, Amanda & Katie}}</ref>}}
[[File:ZettJukassa-ChromeBlack2023.png|thumb|left|250px|Zett Jukassa was portrayed by Jett Lucas.]]
[[Jett Lucas]], son of ''[[Star Wars]]'' creator [[George Lucas]], portrayed Zett Jukassa<ref name="StarWars.com" /> in the [[2002]] [[prequel trilogy]] film, [[Star Wars: Episode II Attack of the Clones|''Star Wars'': Episode II ''Attack of the Clones'']],<ref name="Episode II" /> as well as the [[2005]] film [[Star Wars: Episode III Revenge of the Sith|''Star Wars'': Episode III ''Revenge of the Sith'']], where he was first identified in its credits.<ref name="Episode III" /> In a deleted sequence from Episode II, Jukassa walks by Obi-Wan Kenobi on a flight of stairs and nods at him. Around twenty takes of the scene were shot.<ref name="Deleted">{{YouTube|video=TH2h0HIv108|text=Sandtroopers Interrogation: Meet Jett Lucas|channel=channel/UC5swyobh8zpArOmGr4DfnYQ|name=sandtroopersDOTcom}}</ref> The character's name was changed several times during production of Episode III; his alternate names included Titi Jukassa, Tado Jukassa, and simply Tado. Ultimately, it was decided that he would be known as Zett Jukassa.<ref name="DB">{{DB|character|zettjukassa|Jukassa, Zett}}</ref> His scene for ''Revenge of the Sith''&mdash;which was numbered 113&mdash;was filmed on Monday, [[July 28]], [[2003]] on Stage 5 at [[Shepperton Studios]]. The set was raised and filmed on a bluescreen.<ref name="Making">''[[The Making of Star Wars Revenge of the Sith]]''</ref>

For the role, Lucas trained with stunt coordinators [[Nick Gillard]] and [[Kyle Rowling]] on how to use his lightsaber to fight against the digitally created clone troopers. Before they taught him more complicated moves, they began with basic techniques such as sword twirling. For Jukassa's flip, Gillard originally intended to have Lucas perform it in wires. While the scene was indeed recorded in that manner, Lucas was later asked to jump and pretend to land, with the rest being done digitally. George Lucas's direction for Jukassa was to act angry for the scene. Gillard, as well as Lucas's sister, [[Katie Lucas]], thought that Jett did quite well in his portrayal of Jukassa.<ref name="StarWars.com" />

In the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] continuity, Lucas chose for his character in Episode II to be known as Padawan Warpoc Skamini,<ref name="DB" /> though after the release of Episode III, the two characters were merged into one via a backstory<ref name="StarWars.com" /> revealed in "[[Order 66: Destroy All Jedi]]," a magazine article written by [[Daniel Wallace]] and published in the [[Star Wars Insider 87|87th issue]] of the ''[[Star Wars Insider]]'' magazine<ref name="Warpoc">{{InsiderCite|87|Order 66: Destroy All Jedi}}</ref> on [[April 17]], [[2006]].<ref name="April">{{SWArchive|url=community/fanclub/mag/news20060406.html|text=Inside ''Star Wars Insider'' #87}}</ref> Wallace did not remember where the Skamini name originated from.<ref name="Wallace">{{Twitter|danwallaceMSP|status/1400895148632936448|[[Daniel Wallace]]|quote=Almost positive it's not my creation, but also can't recall where I lifted that backstory info from.|archivedate=20210607220323}}</ref> Jukassa's [[StarWars.com]] [[Databank (2014-)|Databank]] entry confirmed that the two roles were still intended to be one character in the new ''Star Wars'' [[canon]].<ref name="DB Zett" />

